From: emscripten-forge
Subject: [PATCH] Figures drawn with Java2D when OpenGL is not available

With -Dscilab.graphics.renderer=java2d, the figure canvas is a Swing
component drawing the figure with SciRenderer's G2D implementation (the
one the vectorial exports use) into an image, instead of a JoGL
GLJPanel/GLCanvas: SwingView does not initialize JoGL, the clipboard,
image export and bitmap exports use the component's image, and the G2D
canvas serializes drawing (its scene is static). Java code does not load
JoGL classes for direct buffers anymore.
